sub:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-058> pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-058-overall> .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-058-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Thompson (1917) Cartesian transformation of the human skull into chimpanzee, baboon and dog (Figs. 404-408) — MorphoEval overall 62.1/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-28"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "v1 reconstructs Thompson's human->chimpanzee net as a TPS (bending energy 2.10, affine determinant 0.54, net-alignment RMS 1.02 grid units) and warps the Fig. 404 drawing through it, visually reproducing Fig. 406. Applied to the 11 human landmarks of Fig. 404 the net removes 35 % of the Procrustes distance to a real chimpanzee skull (0.383 -> 0.249; affine part alone 0.430, i.e. -12 %), 24 % toward the baboon, 22 % toward the dog and -27 % toward the human specimen (T is a prognathism direction that helps every non-human target, most for the chimpanzee). Direction cosine between Thompson's drawn displacement and the real human->chimp displacement 0.73. Cell-area field of the net: log-linear R^2 0.95, beta_i +0.40 (behind->forwards), beta_j -0.61 (upwards), 5.7x front/back, 7.4x bottom/top. Real specimens: d_P(H,C) 0.315 < d_P(H,B) 0.505 < d_P(H,D) 0.603; cos(chimp,baboon) 0.78, cos(chimp,dog) 0.78, k_baboon/k_chimp 1.25; facial index 0.48/0.66/1.27/0.61 and facial angle 89/68/56/45 deg for H/C/B/D. Verdict by the script's 11 binary checks: 9/11 (\"supported\") - but without any uncertainty quantification. Overall 62.2/100. Overall 62.1/100 (faithfulness 56.1, reproducibility 76.3); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 6475519d7; environment: . Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 70, Morphological realism / specimen match 55, Parameter expressivity 40, Morphometric validation 50, Source and data traceability 85, Code-to-model traceability 75, Reproducibility package 70. Output judged: docs/media/t1917_058_on_the_theory_of_transformatio_comparison.png: rendered output of thompson/claims/t1917-058_on-the-theory-of-transformations.py at 6475519d7, image/png, 1125970 B, 1980×1210 px, artifact_sha256 af29c319c321f54e0a3e20afadd5a29270bc96b1373db6d9035ede0023daa436 (sha256 af29c319c321f54e0a3e20afadd5a29270bc96b1373db6d9035ede0023daa436), spec_fingerprint 974f3b1907dd69da0acb085b9f36dedce4c4532b025e0bf27519cd77a4567dc9. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 974f3b1907dd69da0acb085b9f36dedce4c4532b025e0bf27519cd77a4567dc9; artifact_sha256: af29c319c321f54e0a3e20afadd5a29270bc96b1373db6d9035ede0023daa436; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-058/canis_familiaris_lateral.jpg=e5b1eab566faf5ed..., datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-058/fig404_human_skull_cartesian.jpg=568644185cca883a..., datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-058/fig405_chimpanzee_coordinates.jpg=7314ff685861068f..., datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-058/homo_sapiens_lateral.jpg=3457d096022c4b4f..., datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-058/pan_troglodytes_lateral.jpg=04455ef234b6ac4a..., datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-058/paper_citations.bib=f2b7ee8ec50937e4..., datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-058/papio_ursinus_lateral.jpg=02e80d49035d3940..., datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-058/scout_manifest.json=4aab29fefc62323b..., datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-058/t1917_058_on_the_theory_of_transformatio_reference.json=4fdcd4cba2786813...}. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Thompson (1917) pp. 770-773: the human skull drawn in a 5x4 Cartesian net (Fig. 404) and the chimpanzee, baboon and dog skulls drawn in deformed nets (Figs. 405-408); prose statements that the deformation is one 'harmonious and congruent transformation', that cell areas increase 'in approximately logarithmic order' from above downwards and behind forwards, that the baboon differs 'only in an increased intensity', that the chimpanzee is 'much nearer the human type than the baboon', and that the dog's net 'tapers away in front' on 'different lines'.; reconstructed_in_script: The Fig. 405 net digitised (skeleton junctions + 4 manual corners), reconstructed as a thin-plate spline T in human grid units (E1-E3); cell-area log-linear regression (E4); 11 homologous landmarks digitised by the loop agent on Fig. 404, Fig. 406 and four Commons specimens; full-Procrustes explained fraction of T(H) toward the real chimpanzee (E6); displacement-field cosines and intensity ratios between real specimens; facial index and Camper-type facial angle (E7).; transfer_boundary: One specimen per taxon (museum photographs for chimpanzee, baboon, dog; a rendered anatomical model for the human); the baboon and dog nets of Figs. 407-408 were not digitised, so sub-claims C2/C5 are tested on real specimens only, not on Thompson's drawings of them.; does_not_claim: Nothing about growth, ontogeny or phylogeny; no claim that Thompson's particular curves are the optimal smooth map; the 'supported' verdict of v1 carries no confidence interval (remediation R1).." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/claude-fable-5.1> ;
        pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
        pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: {'id': 'R1', 'item': 'Propagate landmark-digitisation uncertainty: jitter bootstrap (sigma 1.5 % centroid size, 1000 reps) for the explained fraction, facial indices and distance ordering; add a permutation null for E_C; report r, RMSE and a KS test on per-landmark residuals'}",
            "remediation needed: {'id': 'R2', 'item': 'Run and report the parameter-regime sweep: lambda in {0, 1e-3, 1e-2, 1e-1, 1} (affine limit) and k in {0, 0.5, 1, 1.5, 2, 2.5}; show E and the predicted facial angle as monotone functions of k'}",
            "remediation needed: {'id': 'R3', 'item': 'Add negative / ablation controls: affine-only ablation already present - add a label-shuffled null, a mirrored (anti-Thompson) net and a wrong-target specificity index'}",
            "remediation needed: {'id': 'R4', 'item': \"Computer-vision segmentation of the four specimen photographs (Otsu silhouette on the grey museum background) -> silhouette height profile and taper index to test the dog 'triangular conformation' criterion (C5) instead of the tied displacement cosines; also a silhouette face fraction\"}",
            "remediation needed: {'id': 'R5', 'item': 'Replace or supplement the rendered human model with a museum photograph of a real Homo sapiens skull; report drawing-fidelity (Fig. 404 vs specimen) alongside the headline'}",
            "remediation needed: {'id': 'R6', 'item': 'Independent second assessor (different provider) - this round is builder-scored'}" ;
        pk:hasScore "0.621"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/claude-fable-5.1> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Claude Fable 5.1 (builder-assessor, single-agent Pass 1; second assessor pending)" ;
        dct:identifier "claude-fable-5.1" ;
        prov:actedOnBehalfOf <https://orcid.org/0009-0007-4948-9192> .
}

